NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001683 "=head1 CREDITS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001684 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001685 "Versions through 0.59 (and much of this documentation) were written by:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001686 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001687 "Mark-Jason Dominus"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001688 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001689 "This version borrows some documentation and routine names from"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001690 "Mark-Jason's, but Diff.pm's code was completely replaced."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001691 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001692 "This code was adapted from the Smalltalk code of Mario Wolczko"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001693 "<mario@wolczko.com>, which is available at"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001694 "ftp://st.cs.uiuc.edu/pub/Smalltalk/MANCHESTER/manchester/4.0/diff.st"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001695 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001696 "C<sdiff> and C<traverse_balanced> were written by Mike Schilli"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001697 "<m@perlmeister.com>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001698 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001699 "The algorithm is that described in"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001700 "I<A Fast Algorithm for Computing Longest Common Subsequences>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001701 "CACM, vol.20, no.5, pp.350-353, May 1977, with a few"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001702 "minor improvements to improve the speed."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001703 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001704 "Much work was done by Ned Konz (perl@bike-nomad.com)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001705 ""
